  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the User\'s Request**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s request for the \"IMS \342\200\223 Institute Management System\" blueprint, specifically the v1.0.0-MVP. My focus is initially on the architecture and design system. I\'ve started by examining the color palette, noting the primary color `#1E3A8A`. I am gathering all these details to see all the request details.\n\n\n**Defining the UI Elements**\n\nI\'ve moved on to solidify the UI elements, including a detailed color palette with hover states and a sans-serif font paired with JetBrains Mono for specific numeric data. Next, I am thinking through the RBAC structure, starting with SUPER_ADMIN and ADMIN roles. I\'m noting specific web routes and mobile screen previews for each.\n\n\n**Mapping Feature Implementation**\n\nI\'m now mapping out features for the IMS blueprint, focusing on batch and timetable management, fees, and the notice board. I\'m visualizing weekly scheduler matrices and capacity gauges. I\'ve also incorporated the user\'s role-based access control (RBAC) details, specifically the web routes and mobile screen previews for both the teacher and student roles. I\'m prioritizing user experience throughout.\n\n\n**Outlining Core Components**\n\nI\'m now identifying specialized components for the student and parent modules. I\'m focusing on the `StatCard` for KPIs with trend indicators and the `PerformanceTrendChart` for analytics. This is to solidify the structure of the system and user interaction.\n\n\n\n**Detailing Specific UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI-specific elements for student performance analysis. I\'m focusing on a dual-line chart to compare student scores to class averages, alongside an attendance heatmap and an at-risk badge system to swiftly identify students needing intervention. I\'m also planning a \'FastAttendanceGrid\' for quick attendance marking, complete with hotkeys and streak calculations. A badge system will be added to the gamification aspect.\n\n\n"
