    thinking: "**Constructing Mock Data**\n\nI\'m now focused on building the `/src/data/mockData.ts` file. My goal is to create comprehensive, interlinked mock data encompassing all five roles. Currently, I\'m starting with the Institute, \"Apex National Institute of Science & Technology\" (ANIST) and its \"ANIST-HQ\" code, including its four campuses in South Bay and North Metro.\n\n\n**Defining User Personas**\n\nI\'ve just added detailed user personas to my mock data. I\'ve defined a `u-superadmin` and `u-admin` users, along with several teachers and students, and even a parent, each with specific details like roles, names, and even student roll numbers and grade levels. I\'m focusing on making these characters realistic, which is crucial for testing. I also defined an honor and regular batch.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing out \"Batch Gamma\", a Grade 12 advanced pre-med group. I\'m focusing on adding courses like physics, math, and chemistry, with specific topics. I\'m building out mock data including attendance records for various students, detailed test results for performance analysis, and homework submissions with statuses. Furthermore, I\'m integrating fee invoices with payment statuses and creating performance alerts and improvement plans to add more realistic, actionable insights for the user.\n\n\n"
