    thinking: "**Analyzing the Provided Data**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the attached file, \"TuitionPro__Coaching_Class_Manager_0bb8e5d0.html,\" and the user\'s feedback. I\'m carefully dissecting the user\'s points about missing data and the app\'s need for responsive screen sizes, to understand exactly what needs to be addressed.\n\n\n**Addressing Screen Size Concerns**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user\'s explicit request for viewport switching controls into the app. My plan is to offer presets such as iPhone, Tablet, and Desktop views, or to achieve a native feel by default. I am leveraging the existing responsive styles present in the provided HTML. I\'m focusing on ensuring this feature integrates seamlessly and delivers a smooth experience.\n\n\n**Implementing Viewport Switcher**\n\nI am now planning the implementation of a top bar viewport switcher, offering options like \"Mobile App (390px)\", \"Tablet App (768px)\", and \"Full Screen / Responsive Desktop\". This will enable users to instantly change the entire app view into a simulated mobile environment or a fully responsive layout. This will incorporate a mobile-first, responsive design, along with flex-column arrangements, bottom/top navigation, and touch optimizations, to solve the screen size concern.\n\n**Data Assessment Underway**\n\nI am now beginning to examine the data within `TuitionPro__Coaching_Class_Manager_0bb8e5d0.html`. Specifically, I have found `inq`, which relates to Inquiries / Leads / Admissions, and I am noting the inclusion of Inquiries with Name, Phone, Course, Source, Assigned Staff, Follow-up Date, and Status (New, Contacted, Demo Scheduled, Follow-Up, Admitted, Lost). I am also finding data such as follow-up trackers and conversion rate metrics. I am also planning to look at \'mat\'.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Exploration**\n\nI\'m now delving into additional data categories. I\'m focusing on Parent-Teacher Meetings (`ptm`), with details like date, time, location, and batch. I\'m also examining `fin`, the finance ledger, noting debit/credit entries, categories, amounts, and modes, including the net operating balance. Next, I\'m analyzing `sl`, for Timetables, with conflict detection and substitute teacher assignment, and `att` for Biometric Attendance, including import features. I am keeping `fee` for last.\n\n\n**Exploring Additional Data Categories**\n\nI\'m now examining several more data components. I\'m focusing on the reminders features, including due date configuration and one-click reminders for parents with pending fees, receipt generation, and batch-wise and monthly collections breakdowns. I\'m also now analyzing the student master (`stu`), including class, parent/guardian details, fee breakdowns, and attendance metrics. I\'m planning to look into courses and batches (`courses & batches`), staff accounts and permitted modules (`staff`), audit history (`audit`), and demo/institute visit feedback (`fbk`) for further understanding.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Feature Refinement**\n\nI\'m currently prioritizing enhancements based on the user\'s feedback. I\'m focusing on the newly identified areas. I am making sure the new version is more comprehensive than the existing one, with features like an inquiry lead CRM, a content library, a PTM scheduler, an institute finance ledger, substitute teacher assignment, biometric attendance import, device viewport mode, and Indian Rupees (\342\202\271) formatting.\n\n\n**Integrating TuitionPro Data**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on integrating all TuitionPro data and modules with the existing IMS architecture. I am ensuring that no data is left behind. I will be looking closely at the types defined in `/src/types/ims.ts`. Specifically, I will enrich this file to include schemas for Inquiries, StudyMaterial, PTMs, FinanceEntry, SubstituteAssignment, and DemoFeedback. I am also working on adding the viewport size type: `mobile | tablet | desktop`.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
