  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Marks & Results**\n\nI\'m now diving into the \"Marks & Results\" tab. Currently, I\'m examining the components there: the marks entry card with its dropdowns, inputs, and buttons, along with the result leaderboard. The next step is incorporating a visual grade distribution chart using Recharts to enhance the tab\'s data presentation.\n\n\n**Integrating Grade Distribution**\n\nI\'m focusing now on integrating the grade distribution chart. I am currently working on the chart\'s data structure using the test results, filtering by the current exam. I\'m calculating grade counts based on percentage ranges from marks and mapping them to a data structure compatible with Recharts. I plan to present this visually near the results leaderboard.\n\n\n**Calculating Grade Distribution**\n\nI\'ve completed the grade distribution calculation and have the data structured. It uses the `examResults` to generate counts for each grade (A+ to F), then it calculates the pass rate. I\'m now focusing on how best to visually represent this data using Recharts\' BarChart3 component.\n\n\n**Visualizing Exam Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating exam data visualization. I\'m focusing on incorporating a Recharts bar chart to graphically display exam results data. I\'m currently working to create data suitable for chart. The data will show passing count and total evaluated, along with grade summaries. I\'m thinking of how to display counts for each grade (A+ to F), within a `grid` layout.\n\n\n**Refining Chart Display**\n\nI\'m currently refining the chart display, now that it renders. I\'m focusing on the `BarChart` configuration using `Recharts`, customizing tooltips and labels to enhance clarity. I\'m adjusting colors and tick parameters for improved visual appeal and readability, and I want a clean, minimalist aesthetic. I\'m also ensuring the chart is responsive using `ResponsiveContainer`.\n\n\n"
